  "details": "ShuffleArray sometimes causes \"Index was outside the bounds of the array\" exception with a very low probability. And it halts the UdonBehavior.\nThere was [an explanation of ShuffleArray](https://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/449386885299830794/848015204729880576) on the main discord. If this is actual source code, the IndexOutOfRangeException could happen. Because `Random.value` range is \"0.0 [inclusive] and 1.0 [inclusive]\" (from [API reference](https://docs.unity3d.com/2019.4/Documentation/ScriptReference/Random-value.html)). So if `Random.value` returns `1.0`,  `int r` becomes `n` that is out of the range.\nI think straight forward implementation of [Fisher–Yates shuffle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fisher%E2%80%93Yates_shuffle) will fix this issue like this:\n```\npublic static void ShuffleArray<T>(T[] array)\n{\n    int n = array.Length;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - 2; i++)\n    {\n        int r = Random.Range(i, n);\n        T t = array[r];\n        array[r] = array[i];\n        array[i] = t;\n    }\n}\n```\nNote: ureishi-san originally [found this issue](https://twitter.com/aivrc/status/1455088819405942785). What a great job again!",
